<p>Israeli air strikes across Lebanon killed at least 39 people on Saturday, Lebanon&#x27;s Health Ministry said, despite a U.S.-brokered ceasefire between Israel and Hezbollah. Three drone strikes on vehicles south of Beirut killed four people. Strikes in southern Lebanon killed others, including at least seven people in Saksakiyeh, where the ministry said a child was among the dead and 15 people were wounded. Israel&#x27;s military said it struck Hezbollah operatives and infrastructure, including more than 85 Hezbollah targets over the previous 24 hours, and said explosive drones launched by Hezbollah wounded three Israeli reservists near the border. Hezbollah said its attacks responded to Israeli ceasefire violations and attacks on Lebanese villages.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/BKV2Dlcil0ZvxjjrvqlDaFQDS57XqMpdsMWwIFMKorSc4vDFgcNxTEP7VWi8-G-NH1pYx0BJMMeEAtaOMFs1IL20LmeBgEQ636J6Nt0poszg-GvhAUN0Sykgr-bReXLyxckYjEAU4H8IxyatzHnTqaPrgSbX62YJc8w7NNjRAf5O8pfgyfBeMe8KCHxJy-LyvXkhC9NQ3Wp7PRuUtmj19AkjBXlQUdhI' alt='Rescue workers searching for survivors under the rubble of houses damaged by an Israeli airstrike Saturday, in the village of Saksakiyeh in southern Lebanon.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Evacuation warnings: The Israeli military told residents of nine southern Lebanese villages to evacuate and said it would act “forcefully” against Hezbollah.</li><li>Nabatieh strike: Lebanon&#x27;s Health Ministry said a drone hit a Syrian man and his 12-year-old daughter on a motorcycle in Nabatieh, then struck again after they moved from the first site.</li><li>Civilian review: The Israeli military said it was reviewing reports of harm to uninvolved civilians in Saksakiyeh after saying it had targeted Hezbollah militants operating from a building used for military purposes.</li><li>Border damage: Lebanon&#x27;s state-run National News Agency reported Israeli artillery fire and home demolitions in several southern towns, including Bint Jbeil&#x27;s Al-Jabana n